import Mathlib

/-!
# `∏_{p < 10⁴} (1 + (p^{−2/3} + p^{−1/3})/(p − 1)) ≤ 7.99`, checked by the kernel

A table `PK` of pairs `(p, k_p)` (generated by `scripts/gen_prod_ap.py`) lists the primes `p < 10⁴` with
`k_p ≥ 10⁶ p^{−1/3}` (`p k_p³ ≥ 10¹⁸`). The kernel (`decide +kernel`) checks:
* every `p` in the table is prime (no divisor `2 ≤ d ≤ 100`, `d² ≤ p`) and `p k_p³ ≥ 10¹⁸`;
* every `n < 10⁴` not in the table is not prime (`n < 2` or it has a divisor in `[2, n)`);
* `∏ (1 + (r² + r)/(p − 1)) ≤ 7.99` for `r = k_p/10⁶`, in exact rational arithmetic.
-/

